        <body>
            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="0750" n="742" xml:id="pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12114: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-16T16:00:00+02:00">June 16, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>705. The military news from Syria today Rochat said confirms that the French have
                    withdrawn north of Sidon but that their positions there seem strong; in other
                    areas the French are even counterattacking he claimed. He admitted that the
                    German “offer” to send military assistance—of what specific sort he did not
                    know—to the French defence of Syria is becoming more “insistent”. He is pleased
                    as are our other friends in the Foreign Office that the French Government has
                    firmly declined this “offer”: they feel that France’s moral position will be
                    much stronger even if Syria is lost, (and they probably realize that it would be
                    lost to France anyway if Germany does occupy the territory, whether to send
                    assistance or otherwise).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
